{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Not because you are numerous.</b> As its plain sense; and its midrash — because you do not make yourselves great when I bestow good upon you, therefore <b>He desired … you</b>." "<b>For you are the fewest.</b> You diminish yourselves — like Abraham, who said (Genesis 18) ״וְאָנֹכִי עָפָר וָאֵפֶר״, and like Moses and Aaron, who said (Exodus 16) ״וְנַחְנוּ מָה״ — not like Nebuchadnezzar, who said (Isaiah 14) ״אֶדַּמֶּה לְעֶלְיוֹן״, and Sennacherib (ibid. 36), who said ״מִי בְּכָל אֱלֹהֵי הָאֲרָצוֹת״, and Hiram, who said (ibid. 28) ״אֵל אָנִי מוֹשַׁב אֱלֹהִים יָשַׁבְתִּי״ (Ḥullin 9)." "<b>For you are the fewest.</b> Here כִּי serves in the sense of דְּהָא ['for indeed']."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:17.255737134Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}